					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tl333s" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1304786); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1304786&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608349761" alt="TL333s" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1304786)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tl333s" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1304786); return false;" >TL333s</a></span> <span class="odate time_1390609574 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">25 Jan 2014 00:26</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1945518">
									

<p>I like how this could have been just another of those ineffable &quot;wise mystic words about Ancient Unknowable Things&quot; entries, and we all would have nodded and hmm'd and been very confused about what was said and unwilling to admit it. But then in comes this snarky little shit (it's Saturn Deer? Makes <em>all</em> the sense) to fill us in on the gaps and take some piss out of the guy. And what works best about that is his attitude of &quot;Yeah, he's nuts, and kind of full of himself, but he has seen and done and met some Shit, and I gotta respect that.&quot; So it's not all mockery, but instead gives a sense that, yeah, he's seen some of this stuff too.</p>
<p>Also, I am just pleased as punch to even see the world &quot;Alexylva&quot;. Whatever happened to that GoI? I'm so sad it's fallen out of favor over the last year or so, it's one of my favorites. I imagine it's just very hard to write for.</p>

							</div>

								
					
