														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1947121">
									

<p>This reads to me a lot like Divine Comedy in reverse. Not saying that's a bad thing, just noting it here.</p>
<p>After the first three or so, Deer's annotations turn from actual substantial commentary/translation, to just cheeky remarks. This saddens me.</p>
<p>Neutral vote on this. I like the mythology that was set up in Dust and Blood, but within this mythology, the journey described here is kind of stereotypical and bland, and there wasn't enough Deer to compensate for that.</p>

